                            <comment id="16348493" author="agura" created="Thu, 1 Feb 2018 12:19:38 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=lexa&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;lexa&quot;&gt;lexa&lt;/a&gt; Could you please share performance measurement result before fix and with fix? What about other WAL modes: BACKGROUND and LOG_ONLY?&lt;br/&gt;
Is it possible that TX_RECORDS added to the WAL affects performance, not WAL optimizations itself?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16348575" author="lexa" created="Thu, 1 Feb 2018 13:30:12 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=agura&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;agura&quot;&gt;agura&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;tx-putAll have drop ~ 50% between your commit and previous.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;another tx benchmarks have drop ~ 10-15%&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;In BackGround mode we don&apos;t have drop between this commits.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;I don&apos;t have counts for LOG_ONLY and this commits. But between 2.3 and 2.4 branches we have increase ~ x10. e.x. 4 servers 8 clients atomic-put in 2.3 ~ 5700 per client in seconds and in 2.4 ~ 53000 per client in seconds.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
</comment>
                            <comment id="16376904" author="ilantukh" created="Mon, 26 Feb 2018 14:01:55 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Temporary resolved performance drop by restoring old WAL implementation (before &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-6339&quot; title=&quot;WAL: Avoid closed by interruption exception when user thread is interrupted&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;IGNITE-6339&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;IGNITE-6339&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;) and using it in FSYNC WAL mode.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16378233" author="agura" created="Tue, 27 Feb 2018 08:33:39 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Thanks, Ilya. I created new ticket for performance drop investigation: &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-7820&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-7820&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
